.*
.* QTOCAPP: CFGTCPAPP and the applications' own menus (CFGTCPSNMP,
.* CFGTCPRTD, CFGTCPBP, CFGTCPTELN, CFGTCPSMTP). An option whose
.* command this release does not have answers that it is not available.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGTCPAPP HELP=HLPAPP KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Configure TCP/IP Applications
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=IND OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPSNMP'.Configure SNMP agent
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPRTD'.Configure RouteD
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPBP'.Configure BOOTP
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='CMD ?CHGDDMTCPA'.Change DDM TCP attributes
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='CMD ?CHGFTPA'.Change FTP attributes
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPTELN'.Configure TELNET
:MENUI OPTION=12 ACTION='CMD CFGTCPSMTP'.Configure SMTP
:MENUI OPTION=13 ACTION='CMD ?CHGLPDA'.Change LPD attributes
:MENUI OPTION=16 ACTION='CMD ?CHGPOPA'.Change POP attributes
:MENUI OPTION=17 ACTION='CMD ?CHGRXCA'.Change REXEC attributes
:MENUI OPTION=19 ACTION='CMD ?CHGNTPA'.Change SNTP attributes
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGSNMP HELP=HLPSNMP KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Configure TCP/IP SNMP
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD ?CHGSNMPA'.Change SNMP attributes
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD ADDCOMSNMP'.Work with communities for SNMP
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGRTD HELP=HLPRTD KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Configure TCP/IP RouteD
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD WRKRTDCFG'.Work with RouteD configuration
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGBP HELP=HLPBP KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Configure TCP/IP BOOTP
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD WRKBPTBL'.Work with BOOTP table
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGTELN HELP=HLPTELN KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Configure TCP/IP TELNET
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=IND OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUGRP.Work with associated system values:
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL SYSVAL(QAUTOVRT)'.Autoconfigure virtual devices
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL SYSVAL(QLMTSECOFR)'.Limit security officer device access
:MENUI OPTION=12 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL SYSVAL(QINACTITV)'.Inactive job time-out
:MENUI OPTION=13 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL SYSVAL(QINACTMSGQ)'.Inactive job message queue
:MENUI OPTION=14 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL SYSVAL(QLMTDEVSSN)'.Limit device sessions
:MENUI OPTION=15 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL SYSVAL(QMAXSGNACN)'.Action to take for failed sign-on attempts
:MENUI OPTION=16 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL SYSVAL(QMAXSIGN)'.Maximum sign-on attempts allowed
:MENUI OPTION=17 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL SYSVAL(QRMTSIGN)'.Remote sign-on control
:MENUI OPTION=18 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL SYSVAL(QDEVRCYACN)'.Device I/O error action
:MENUI OPTION=19 ACTION='CMD WRKSYSVAL SYSVAL(QDSCJOBITV)'.Time interval before disconnected jobs end
:EMENUGRP.
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=CFGSMTP HELP=HLPSMTP KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Configure TCP/IP SMTP
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD WRKNAMSMTP'.Work with system alias table
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD WRKNAMSMTP'.Work with personal alias table
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPAPP.Configure TCP/IP Applications - Help
:P.The applications that run over TCP/IP: their attributes and the
menus that set them up. An application this release does not have yet
says so when its option is chosen.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPSNMP.Configure TCP/IP SNMP - Help
:P.The SNMP agent's attributes and communities.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPRTD.Configure TCP/IP RouteD - Help
:P.The RouteD server's configuration.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPBP.Configure TCP/IP BOOTP - Help
:P.The BOOTP server's table of clients.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPTELN.Configure TCP/IP TELNET - Help
:P.The system values the TELNET server works by: how virtual devices are
made, which sessions are allowed, how long idle jobs stay and what a
lost connection does to its job.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=HLPSMTP.Configure TCP/IP SMTP - Help
:P.The alias tables mail is addressed through.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
